("P", "Propagation (EQ:psi) is anisotropic. Each burning neighbor $(i,j)$ in the eight-neighborhood $\\mathcal{N}_8$ contributes its rate of spread $R_k$ weighted by the cosine of the angle between the wind direction $W_{wd,k}$ and the direction $\\varphi_{ij}$ to the target cell, and $R_k$ is the Rothermel-type map $f_{ros}$ of (EQ:ros) over wind, slope, aspect, moisture, and fuel type {6}. The front advances in substeps, so spread never exceeds one cell per substep. Spotting is the only stochastic element and is driven by the seeded random stream. Precipitation raises $F_{moist,k}$ toward the extinction level with a time constant of about thirty minutes, so a front dies out gradually."),
